        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="0845" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg759"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-09-15"><hi rendition="#italic">September 15,
                            1903</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Leishman reports that during a conversation on September 14 the grand vizier
                    showed quite plainly a determination to resist, as far as possible, the
                    settlement of any cases except the Beirut affair under pressure of presence of
                    the United States squadron.</p>
                <p>Mr. Leishman states that he will continue gentle but firm pressure, but that it
                    may become necessary to resort to sterner language in order to bring the Ottoman
                    Government to a fuller realization of their obligations.)</p>
            </div>
